WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.300
The past

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.302
12 months have been pretty chaotic

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.436
for Rupert Murdoch,

00:00:03.436 --> 00:00:06.439
and it goes beyond this high stakes case.

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:08.441
Vanity Fair's Gabriel Sherman

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:09.876
has the behind the scenes

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:11.711
reporting on the billionaire's

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:13.079
media moguls,

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:14.581
health problems, his divorce,

00:00:14.581 --> 00:00:15.949
a broken engagement

00:00:15.949 --> 00:00:16.916
and a real life

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:19.152
succession battle among his kids.

00:00:19.586 --> 00:00:22.155
There's even signs that a hit HBO show

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:25.692
has been getting under his skin.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:28.161
Dad's gone.

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.362
We have to trust each other.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:30.797
What about me?

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:31.664
Don't lie to me.

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:33.900
I got a lot of options.

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.703
Well, Sherman has been struck

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:38.471
by how diminished

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:39.706
Murdoch's own influence

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:41.508
has been after the 2020 election writing.

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:42.842
Rupert called Trump

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:44.210
before Biden's inauguration

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:46.246
to tell him to accept defeat graciously,

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:47.213
the source said.

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:48.014
Trump refused.

00:00:48.014 --> 00:00:49.783
Trump threatened to start his own channel

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:51.451
and put Fox out of business.

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:52.118
The source said

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:53.286
Murdoch seemed trapped

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:55.655
by the people he radicalized.

00:00:55.655 --> 00:00:57.290
Gabriel Sherman joins us now.

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:58.591
He's a special correspondent

00:00:58.591 --> 00:00:59.492
at Vanity Fair.

00:00:59.492 --> 00:01:01.428
And you can read

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:02.395
the article in Vanity Fair,

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:03.396
RT.com and Vanity

00:01:03.396 --> 00:01:04.831
Fair's May issue,

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:07.200
which hits newsstands on May 2nd.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:08.234
Good morning to you.

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.003
We're so happy that you're here.

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:12.472
So this has been going on for

00:01:13.039 --> 00:01:13.940
quite some time.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.042
It's more than just the Dominion case.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.811
So what gives here

00:01:17.811 --> 00:01:20.046
as it relates to Rupert Murdoch?

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:22.615
Does this inform you as to

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:24.551
what may happen with this case?

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:27.420
Yeah.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:28.121
Good morning, guys.

00:01:28.121 --> 00:01:29.222
You know, I

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:30.223
without question,

00:01:30.223 --> 00:01:31.257
I think the fact that they're

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:32.892
in this $1.6 billion

00:01:32.892 --> 00:01:36.429
lawsuit is a result of Rupert Murdoch's

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:38.131
diminished leadership

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:39.265
and the fact that there really has been

00:01:39.265 --> 00:01:41.401
this vacuum at the top of the company

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:43.036
and it allowed

00:01:43.036 --> 00:01:44.671
all of these Dominion falsehoods

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:45.338
and these lies

00:01:45.338 --> 00:01:47.173
to get onto the air or Fox,

00:01:47.173 --> 00:01:49.409
because they put ratings above all else.

00:01:49.409 --> 00:01:51.644
And there was really no adult in the room

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.580
to say that, you know,

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:54.948
we can get the ratings now,

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:55.648
but there'll be long

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.517
term consequences later. Yeah.

00:01:57.517 --> 00:02:00.353
You quote Murdoch as later testifying.

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:01.688
He told Jared Kushner,

00:02:01.688 --> 00:02:02.155
of course,

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:03.389
the former president's son in law.

00:02:03.389 --> 00:02:04.757
Well, the numbers are the numbers.

00:02:04.757 --> 00:02:05.158
When Trump

00:02:05.158 --> 00:02:06.693
was so mad about the Arizona call,

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:07.594
I do think

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:08.962
a diminished Murdoch

00:02:08.962 --> 00:02:10.396
is such a fascinating part

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:11.164
of your reporting,

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:11.464
Gabe,

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.433
that many people certainly don't see that

00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:15.135
he doesn't want people to see.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.636
But you open your piece

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:17.637
saying

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:20.073
Murdoch is trying to prove one last act,

00:02:20.073 --> 00:02:20.907
as in him,

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:22.442
but his erratic performance,

00:02:22.442 --> 00:02:23.877
which is throwing his personal life

00:02:23.877 --> 00:02:25.478
and his media empire into disarray,

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:25.879
has left

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:27.714
even those in his orbit wondering

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:29.949
if he has lost the plot.

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:31.217
I wonder what your answers

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:31.951
to that question

00:02:31.951 --> 00:02:33.286
now that you've reported this out

00:02:34.921 --> 00:02:35.555
Mm hmm.

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:36.089
Yeah.

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.357
No, I think

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:38.158
sort of sadly,

00:02:38.158 --> 00:02:39.826
I read the quote, that quote

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:41.561
you just read answers the question.

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:43.863
You know, Rupert Murdoch just turned 92.

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:47.167
And for so long, he's sort of kept up

00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:48.701
this myth in the media that he's

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:50.470
this all powerful mogul.

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:51.437
And what I learned

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:53.039
after months of reporting

00:02:53.039 --> 00:02:54.908
is that you know, behind the scenes,

00:02:54.908 --> 00:02:55.942
he is really,

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:56.309
you know,

00:02:56.309 --> 00:02:58.711
as his age would suggest, a very old man.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.713
And there's this joke inside

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:02.482
the Murdoch family that,

00:03:02.482 --> 00:03:04.551
you know, 40 might be the new 30,

00:03:04.717 --> 00:03:06.352
but 80 is 80.

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:08.688
And I think what that means is that he

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.089
he is

00:03:10.523 --> 00:03:11.558
his health has been failing

00:03:11.558 --> 00:03:12.625
for a long time.

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:14.160
And I think now we're just catching up

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:14.894
to the fact

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:16.696
that he's a shell of what he used to be.

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:17.063
Yeah.

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:18.932
But Warren Buffett's also 92

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:20.433
and people are still very keenly

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:21.768
listening to what he says

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:22.735
and following his lead.

00:03:22.735 --> 00:03:23.369
So Clive,

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:24.871
whose name Clive Davis,

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:25.605
is still very close,

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:27.373
even more than age itself.

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.442
But I would point out that Warren

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:30.577
Warren Buffett is often,

00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:31.945
you know, he's out giving interviews.

00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:33.313
You know, we really don't yeah.

00:03:33.313 --> 00:03:35.181
Rupert Murdoch in public,

00:03:35.181 --> 00:03:36.516
except Will, you know,

00:03:36.516 --> 00:03:38.051
perhaps at this Dominion trial.

00:03:38.051 --> 00:03:38.251
Yeah.

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:38.985
Can we talk a little bit

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:39.852
more about the Dominion tribe?

00:03:39.852 --> 00:03:41.221
Because you address these revelations

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:42.755
in the court filings

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:44.624
that the damage is done and you write

00:03:45.692 --> 00:03:46.593
in their own words,

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:47.260
Fox hosts

00:03:47.260 --> 00:03:49.028
have been exposed as propagandists.

00:03:49.028 --> 00:03:50.363
If we lose this suit,

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:51.231
it's F-ing bad,

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:52.799
a senior Fox staffer told me.

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:54.534
And you wrote the book on Fox

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:55.501
this is in 2014,

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.603
the loudest voice in the room

00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:57.136
that you wrote.

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:58.071
What else are you hearing from

00:03:58.071 --> 00:04:01.140
inside insiders there

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:02.408
Yeah, no,

00:04:02.408 --> 00:04:03.309
I think this is really

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:05.545
an existential crisis for the network,

00:04:05.545 --> 00:04:07.981
regardless of the financial impact.

00:04:07.981 --> 00:04:09.682
You know, reputationally,

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:11.284
they've been exposed

00:04:11.284 --> 00:04:13.920
the emails that Dominion has

00:04:15.722 --> 00:04:17.523
obtained in their discovery process.

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:18.391
You know, as a reporter

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:19.892
who's covered this world,

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:22.495
I dreamed of getting that kind of inside

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:24.731
look in that access to Fox News.

00:04:24.731 --> 00:04:26.733
And because of the court order, Dominion

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:28.234
was able to get access

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:28.935
to Fox's

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:30.570
internal communications

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:31.638
and it really was

00:04:31.638 --> 00:04:32.972
as bad as you might imagine.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.407
They were, you know, lying

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:35.708
to their audience in private.

00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:37.310
They said Trump was crazy.

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:38.344
And then on the air

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.580
for 24 hours a day, they would say, he's

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:41.514
the greatest thing ever.

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:42.949
So I think

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:45.218
that to me is one of the lasting impacts

00:04:45.218 --> 00:04:46.919
of this trial, regardless of the outcome.

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:47.120
Yeah.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.421
And even all those questioning

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:50.223
about COVID and vaccine, etc.,

00:04:50.223 --> 00:04:50.823
during COVID,

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:51.891
it was you revealed

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:54.260
Murdoch was always following the science

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:56.863
and always being extra careful, you know,

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.064
during COVID.

00:04:58.064 --> 00:04:58.231
Yeah.

00:04:58.231 --> 00:05:01.200
I mean, his is then his then wife,

00:05:02.001 --> 00:05:03.536
Jerri Hall, required

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:05.004
everyone to test before

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:07.440
seeing him wear masks. Excuse me.

00:05:08.875 --> 00:05:09.909
Happens to us all the time.

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:10.209
Yeah.

00:05:10.209 --> 00:05:11.311
I mean, I think the irony,

00:05:11.311 --> 00:05:12.211
the fact that they were

00:05:12.211 --> 00:05:13.446
I think the fact that they were really

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:15.048
just disrespecting their audience

00:05:15.048 --> 00:05:17.550
and saying one thing while doing another,

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:18.651
I think will be, again,

00:05:18.651 --> 00:05:20.486
just the lasting impact of this era.

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:21.854
I just want to end on this.

00:05:21.854 --> 00:05:24.390
The sadness was not striking to you that

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:25.591
gay rights after interviewing

00:05:25.591 --> 00:05:26.225
dozens of people,

00:05:26.225 --> 00:05:27.427
I was struck by how sad

00:05:27.427 --> 00:05:28.461
all the Murdochs seem.

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:29.595
And it made you think like four.

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:30.663
What can I do?

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:31.564
Why do it all?

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:32.665
And one thing,

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:33.533
because you talk about this

00:05:33.533 --> 00:05:35.601
struggle between Lachlan Murdoch

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:36.803
and James Murdoch,

00:05:36.803 --> 00:05:37.870
and you said a senior

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.038
staffer told you that

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:41.207
James Murdoch sees destroying Fox News.

00:05:41.207 --> 00:05:41.941
This is the other brother.

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:42.542
His politics

00:05:42.542 --> 00:05:44.744
don't go along with Rupert and Lachlan.

00:05:44.977 --> 00:05:45.912
He sees destroying

00:05:45.912 --> 00:05:47.980
Fox News is his mission in life.

00:05:48.181 --> 00:05:49.549
When Murdoch is gone,

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:50.950
You think that that could happen?

00:05:50.950 --> 00:05:52.285
Could James take control

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:54.620
and change sort of the trajectory of

00:05:54.687 --> 00:05:55.655
a Fox News

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.559
Yeah, that would depend on him

00:05:59.559 --> 00:06:01.494
winning the support of his two sisters

00:06:01.494 --> 00:06:02.762
because you need

00:06:02.762 --> 00:06:05.131
three out of the four siblings to

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:06.933
to align to change the leadership

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:07.667
and I think

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:09.535
there's really a shadow war

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:12.205
going on behind the scenes for that.

00:06:12.205 --> 00:06:13.439
But I see your point on the sadness.

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:15.541
I mean, all that money, all that power,

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:17.310
and it's destroyed a family.

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:18.010
And I again,

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:19.011
I think there's sort of like

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:20.413
a lesson for everyone there.

